INT. ROYAL OPERA HOUSE - BACKSTAGE - NIGHT (1923)

Ropes, flats, a smell of greasepaint. Gaslight hisses in sconces. Beyond the curtain, an orchestra tunes.

PRIMA DONNA ELVIRA CASTELLANI (40s, glittering gown, feathered headdress) sweeps down the corridor. Around the corner steps her rival, BARONESS LUDMILLA ROSENKRANZ (40s, ermine stole), and the two women stop face to face.

The stage manager, CORNELIUS BLYTHE (50s, pince-nez), hurries between them.

CORNELIUS
Ladies, please. Curtain in five.

ELVIRA
She is in my dressing room.

LUDMILLA
Your dressing room was always mine.

ELVIRA
She stole my feather.

LUDMILLA
She wore it badly.

Elvira lunges; Ludmilla shoves; the two women tangle, pulling at each other's headdresses, and Cornelius is jostled between them.

TANNOY (V.O.)
(through speaking tube)
Mr. Blythe! The Prince has arrived!

CORNELIUS
Not now!

TANNOY (V.O.)
He asks for the leading lady!

ELVIRA
She can be the leading lady --

LUDMILLA
-- over my dead body!

The two freeze, glaring. Cornelius steps between them with both palms out.

CORNELIUS
Ladies. The Prince.

They both smooth their gowns. Elvira smiles. Ludmilla smiles. Both sweep toward the curtain together.
